course: dictionary
lesson: 15492
title: Stubbly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how something feels or looks. «Dad's chin felt stubbly after three days without a shave.» Stubbly tells you what his chin was like: covered in short, rough hairs. You can picture it, and you can feel it in your mind.
explain: Look at the words around stubbly to find its meaning. A shave means cutting off hair, and «three days without a shave» tells you the hair had grown back short. So stubbly means short and rough, not long or curly.
explain: Stubbly can also describe a field. «The farmer walked across the stubbly field after the harvest.» After the crops are cut, short stalks are left in the ground, and they feel rough and prickly. Stubbly is a good word for that too.
fact: Stubbly means covered with short, rough hairs, like a man's chin when he has not shaved.
fact: «Stubbly» can also describe a field covered with short stalks left after a harvest.
fact: Stubbly is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a chin or a field.
fact: The comparative forms are stubblier and stubbliest: «Grandpa's chin was stubblier than Dad's.»
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence: «Dad's chin felt short and rough» still makes sense, so you are right.
exercise: «Dad's chin felt stubbly after three days without a shave.» What does stubbly mean here? | *Covered with short, rough hairs | Wet from the rain | Very long and curly | Smooth and shiny
exercise: «The farmer walked across the stubbly field after the harvest.» What is stubbly describing? | A road with new tarmac | Tall green grass ready to be mown | A pond full of water | *Short stalks left behind after the crop was cut
exercise: «Grandpa rubbed his stubbly chin and laughed.» Find and copy the word that describes Grandpa's chin. | laughed | chin | rubbed | *stubbly
test: «Mum said his stubbly face needed a shave.» What does stubbly tell us about his face? | He has just had a bath | *Short, rough hairs cover it because he has not shaved | He is very tired | He has a new haircut
test: Ayo says stubbly means smooth and soft. Why is Ayo wrong? | Stubbly means smooth and soft | *Stubbly means rough and covered in short hairs | Stubbly means cold | Stubbly means happy
exam: Which phrase uses stubbly correctly? | *a stubbly field of cut wheat | a stubbly smile on a sunny day | a stubbly bowl of warm soup | a stubbly song that makes everyone dance
